# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.venv-1/

# ── Editors / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Build artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Chroma vector store is regeneratable from data/processed/chunks.json via
# `python src/build_vectorstore.py` — it's binary embedding data, not source,
# and would only bloat git history (and grow every time it's rebuilt) if
# committed. Anyone cloning the repo needs to run that script once before
# src/rag_chain.py can retrieve anything.
data/chroma_db/

# LoRA adapter weights are the same story: regeneratable from
# data/finetune/*.jsonl via `python src/train_lora.py` (see its docstring for
# the exact config each run used), and mlx-lm writes a full checkpoint
# snapshot every `--save-every` iterations — adapters/lastmile-lora-v2/ alone
# is ~840MB across 20 checkpoints. adapter_config.json and training_log.json
# (the actual loss curves — the part worth keeping in git) are small and NOT
# ignored; only the .safetensors weight files are. Anyone who wants the
# actual fine-tuned model running needs to re-run train_lora.py once.
adapters/**/*.safetensors
